From: Samsung Z Flip 5 (SM-F7310) Mainline Linux 7.3.5 Bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: Fix SM8550 DPU DSC initial_lines and DSI CMD_CFG0 for S6E3FAC 120Hz OLED

On Qualcomm SM8550 (DPU 9.0 + DSI 6G v2.7) driving the Samsung S6E3FAC
(AMF670BS03) 1080x2640@120Hz Command-Mode DSC 1.1 panel (2 slices of 540x40):

1. dpu_encoder_dsc_initial_line_calc() computes initial_lines = 2
   (ENC_DF_CTRL = 0x257c0002), whereas stock Samsung ABL programs
   initial_lines = 3 (ENC_DF_CTRL = 0x257c0003). Starting rate-buffer drain
   one line too early produces a regular 60x10-pixel staggered dark-cell
   artifact across every 540x40 slice. Clamping initial_lines to >= 3
   eliminates the artifact completely.

2. dsi_ctrl_enable() overwrites REG_DSI_CMD_CFG0 (0x3c) with 0x00000008,
   clearing the hardware-default upper configuration bits 0x06100000
   (including INTERLEAVE_MAX) preserved by stock ABL (0x06100008). Preserve
   bits [27:20] via read-modify-write.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 2 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c          | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -1984,7 +1984,7 @@ dpu_encoder_dsc_initial_line_calc(struct drm_dsc_config *dsc,
 	total_pixels = ssm_delay * 3 + dsc->initial_xmit_delay + 47;
 	if (soft_slice_per_enc > 1)
 		total_pixels += (ssm_delay * 3);
-	return DIV_ROUND_UP(total_pixels, dsc->slice_width);
+	return max_t(u32, 3, DIV_ROUND_UP(total_pixels, dsc->slice_width));
 }
 
 static void dpu_encoder_dsc_pipe_cfg(struct dpu_hw_ctl *ctl,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -851,7 +851,8 @@ static void dsi_ctrl_enable(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host,
 		dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_VID_CFG1, 0);
 	} else {
 		/* Do not swap RGB colors */
-		data = DSI_CMD_CFG0_RGB_SWAP(SWAP_RGB);
+		data = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_CMD_CFG0) & 0x0ff00000;
+		data |= DSI_CMD_CFG0_RGB_SWAP(SWAP_RGB);
 		data |= DSI_CMD_CFG0_DST_FORMAT(dsi_get_cmd_fmt(mipi_fmt));
 		dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_CMD_CFG0, data);
 
